{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_manuals_focus_focus_architecture", "label": "FOCUS architecture", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_view", "label": "View (FOCUS piece)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_orchestrator", "label": "Orchestrator (FOCUS piece)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_use_case", "label": "Use Case (FOCUS piece)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_repository", "label": "Repository (FOCUS piece)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_every_layer_pays_its_own_way", "label": "Every layer pays its own way", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A layer only earns its place if it can point at a verifiable gain that would vanish without it; 'organization' and 'best practices' are not verifiable gains. Used to reject a fifth DTO-mapper layer, folding the translation into the repository instead."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_errors_are_values", "label": "Errors are values", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A failure that is part of the business flow becomes a typed return value (Result); a failure that is not part of the flow (a bug) stays an exception. Infra exceptions are translated exactly once at the repository boundary so throw is never used as control flow inward."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_result_type", "label": "Result type", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_vertical_slices", "label": "Vertical slices / folder layout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Organize by the axis of change: things that change together live together. One flat folder per feature with four role suffixes, so a change request opens one folder instead of many layered ones."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_dry", "label": "DRY (knowledge, not text)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DRY forbids duplicating knowledge, not text. Two similar-looking rules with different owners are accidental duplication and stay separate; the same underlying fact expressed in different shapes must be unified. Rule of three: extract on the third occurrence."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_yagni_kiss", "label": "YAGNI and KISS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Build only what is actually needed now, not what is foreseen; speculative functionality costs build, carry, delay and repair. YAGNI has no opinion on refactors done for internal quality, only on features nobody asked for yet."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_solid", "label": "SOLID as a filter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_cqs", "label": "CQS / CQRS-lite", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_composition_root", "label": "Composition Root / DI", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every dependency comes in through the constructor so a reader can see it and a forgotten dependency is a compile error rather than a runtime failure. Only the Orchestrator and Repository get DI; the View gets ready state, the Use Case gets data as parameters, keeping it a pure function."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_testing_strategy", "label": "Testing per layer", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Test what a piece promises, not how it delivers, because mocks couple tests to implementation. Use cases get pure tests with no double; orchestrators get a flow test with a repository fake; views get a shape test only where a rendering conditional exists; repositories get a fake for every consumer plus one real integration test per driver."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_anti_patterns", "label": "FOCUS anti-patterns (ch.19)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_strangling_legacy", "label": "Strangling legacy by feature", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Migrate legacy code slice by feature, never by layer, because migrating a whole layer first is a big-bang rewrite wearing a new hat. Migration changes structure and a fix changes behavior; never in the same commit."}, {"id": "docs_manuals_focus_mediator_pattern_csharp", "label": "Mediator pattern as orchestrator (C#)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "House adaptation (stakeholder decision, 2026-09-15): a request handler (MediatR, Mediator, Wolverine, Brighter, or hand-written IRequest/IHandler with a dispatcher) plays the role the book gives the BLoC in chapter 13 -- one event in, one handler run, one new state out. The book itself never maps a specific pattern to a FOCUS piece; this mapping is house-specific."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_manuals_focus_focus_architecture", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_view", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_focus_architecture", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_orchestrator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_focus_architecture", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_use_case", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_focus_architecture", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_repository", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_focus_architecture", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_every_layer_pays_its_own_way", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_view", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_orchestrator", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_orchestrator", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_use_case", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_orchestrator", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_repository", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_use_case", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_result_type", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_repository", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_result_type", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_repository", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_errors_are_values", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_manuals_focus_errors_are_values", "target": "docs_manuals_focus_result_type", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/manuals/focus.md"